── SYNTAX ERROR ─────────────────── E0100_function_in_upper_case.lt:1:4  [E0100]

Stilt names a function in lower case, as `area`:

  1 │ fn Area(w: i64, h: i64) -> i64 { w * h }
    │    ^^^^

A function's name is in snake case; `pub` makes it visible outside its module.

To fix it, rename it `area`:

  1 │ fn area(w: i64, h: i64) -> i64 { w * h }
    │    ~~~~
    ┆
  3 │ fn main() / io { print("{area(2, 3)}") }
    │                          ~~~~
